        "reply_text": "I understand that you bought a phone charger that is not working, you have the bill, and the seller's support team has not resolved the issue despite your contact.\n\nYou may bring a product liability action against a product seller for harm caused by a defective product. A manufacturer is liable if the product has a manufacturing defect or does not follow the express warranty.\n\nFirst, you can lodge a grievance through the National Consumer Helpline via their website, phone, or WhatsApp. They may help resolve the issue directly with the company. Second, if the issue remains, you can file a formal complaint with the District Consumer Commission using the e-Daakhil portal.\n\nKeep your bill, any screenshots of your conversations with support, and the product packaging in a safe place as you will need these as proof.\n\nYou should consider speaking with a lawyer if the company refuses to resolve the matter after you have followed the formal complaint procedures.\n\nCould you please provide the name of the company or seller, and the specific model or brand of the charger?\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\nSource: National Consumer Helpline Grievance Redressal Procedure, procedure 1\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\nSource: e-Daakhil Consumer Grievance and Complaint Portal Procedure, procedure 1\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- Specific legal advice on the likelihood of success for your claim\n- Information on specific court fees or local procedures in Lucknow beyond the general e-Daakhil process\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
